// ATTACHING A REMOTE IMAGE, AS A MODELED OPERATION RATHER THAN A SHELL SCRIPT. extdeps.bmc.megarac
// described this API in prose for months and carried no transport, so the first attach against a
// Mt. Collins unit was driven by hand-written curl — the unmodeled realization DESIGN §6 names, and
// the reason the netboot lane could not claim its image was procured through .dag. The service rows
// made the surface reachable; this module is the caller that makes it reached.
//
// EVERY STEP READS BACK, AND THAT IS FORCED BY THE CONTROLLER'S OWN BEHAVIOUR rather than chosen for
// rigour. gunbc.machine_intake_mtcollins1_diskless_boot_receipt records two measured cases of this
// firmware answering HTTP 500 WHILE THE WRITE TOOK EFFECT: PUT media/general (code 16425) with the
// share re-mounting anyway, and stop-media (code 1411) with the following attach succeeding. An
// operation that treated a non-zero exit as refusal would refuse a write that worked, and the caller
// would then retry or abort against a controller whose state had already moved. So success here is
// never an exit status; it is the configurations listing naming the image.
//
// THE IMAGE INDEX IS RESOLVED, NEVER ASSUMED. start-media takes an image_index, and the controller
// assigns indices by its own enumeration of the share — the same file was index 0 on one scan and
// index 1 after another image appeared. A baked index attaches whatever now occupies that slot,
// which on a share holding a memtest ISO and an installer ISO is a silent wrong-boot rather than a
// failure. The index is read from the images listing by matching the image NAME.
//
// THE IMAGES LISTING ENUMERATES WHAT IS AVAILABLE TO ATTACH, NOT WHAT THE SHARE HOLDS, and an
// earlier revision of this module got that exactly backwards in a way worth recording because the
// wrong diagnosis had a dangerous remedy attached to it. Measured on this unit 2026-09-06: with two
// ISOs in the export, /remote/images listed both; after start-media attached one, the listing
// returned ONLY THE OTHER, and the survivor's image_index moved from 1 to 0. The attached image had
// not vanished — it had moved to /remote/configurations, which is where a presented image lives.
//
// THE EARLIER READING WAS THAT THE LISTING IS A CACHE THAT GOES STALE, with the remedy "re-assert
// mount_cd". That remedy appeared to work, and the reason it appeared to work is the problem:
// toggling mount_cd DETACHES EVERYTHING, which is what returns the image to the available pool. A
// remedy that works by undoing the desired state is worse than no remedy, and it was written into
// an operator-facing message on a lane whose entire purpose is hosts booted from that medium.
//
// WHAT THE HAZARD IS, AT THE STRENGTH IT WAS ACTUALLY MEASURED, because an earlier revision of this
// paragraph overstated it in the same breath as retracting an overstatement. It claimed the toggle
// pulls the running root out from under a booted host. That is the MECHANISM — the presented medium
// is withdrawn, and casper reads the read-only lower layer from it on demand rather than from RAM,
// per this lane's own boot receipt — but it is not what was observed. The toggle WAS performed on
// this unit while it was booted from the medium, and the running installer survived it: measured
// afterwards over serial console, still interactive at its own menu. The controller is configured
// rmedia_retry_count 3 / rmedia_retry_interval 15, and the system was idle at a prompt rather than
// reading, either of which may explain the survival.
//
// SO THE HONEST STATEMENT IS THAT THE BLAST RADIUS IS UNQUANTIFIED, not that it is catastrophic and
// not that it is safe. One observation of one idle host is not evidence that a toggle during heavy
// reads is survivable, and the remedy is still wrong for the reason that does not depend on any of
// this: it "fixes" the listing by undoing the attachment the caller asked for.
//
// SO THE ORDER OF READS IS LOAD-BEARING AND CONFIGURATIONS COMES FIRST. Asking the available list
// whether an already-attached image is present is asking the wrong authority a question it answers
// "no" for the one reason that means SUCCESS. That is what made the operation non-idempotent: a
// second converge against a correctly-attached host refused, which for a converge step is the
// failure mode that matters most, since converge is run repeatedly by construction.
// THE CLEANUP OUTCOME IS CARRIED BESIDE THE ATTACH OUTCOME, never folded into it. Whether the
// image attached and whether the session was released are different facts with different owners: a
// successful attach that leaked a session is still a successful attach, and reporting it as a
// failure would hide the thing that worked while a caller retried it and leaked another. The
// controller's session table is finite — this lane exhausted one service's sessions by opening one
// per probe and closing none — so the release has to be observable rather than assumed.
//
// A LOST OR UNCLASSIFIED GET IS NOT A RELEASED SESSION. CloseSession's own exit is discarded on
// purpose (this firmware has answered HTTP 401 on DELETE while an independent probe showed the
// session gone). The standing is the probe that follows, on a route this firmware serves
// (ProbeSessionOnMediaRoute), with curl --fail-with-body plus a trailing `%{http_code}` write-out,
// so a timeout (`000`), a drop, and an HTTP 401 are different stdout. Only a 401/403 after a
// SUCCEEDING probe before the close, under a parsed X-CSRFTOKEN, is evidence the cookie no longer
// authenticates; every other outcome, and any probe that used a sentinel header, stays
// SessionReleaseRefused.
type SessionRelease
  = SessionReleased
  | SessionReleaseRefused { detail: String }
  | SessionReleaseNotAttempted

type MegaRacAttachResult {
  outcome: MegaRacAttachOutcome
  session_release: SessionRelease
}

// THE ONE SUCCESS IS A READY PRESENTATION, AND IT CARRIES HOW IT WAS REACHED AND WHAT WAS SEEN.
// Already-presented, freshly attached and replaced-then-attached are three ROUTES to the same
// verdict, and all three pass the same readiness fold (side chat on gunbc#12425): a name match on
// an already-presented row is not readiness, and was the gap that let a boot power on over a
// presentation that had not started.
type MegaRacAttachOutcome
  = MegaRacPresentationReady { route: MegaRacAttachRoute, evidence: MegaRacPresentationEvidence }
  | MegaRacReadinessTimedOut { image_name: NonEmptyStr, route: MegaRacAttachRoute, last: ReadinessLook, deadline: EpochMs, looks: Int }
  | MegaRacReadinessRefused { image_name: NonEmptyStr, route: MegaRacAttachRoute, look: ReadinessLook, looks: Int }
  | MegaRacReadinessClockUnreadable { image_name: NonEmptyStr, route: MegaRacAttachRoute, detail: String }
  | MegaRacConfigurationsUnreadable { detail: String }
  | MegaRacSessionRefused { detail: String }
  | MegaRacSessionTokenUnreadable { detail: String }
  | MegaRacImagesUnreadable { detail: String }
  | MegaRacImageListingEmpty
  | MegaRacImageListingUnparseable { detail: String }
  | MegaRacImageNotEnumerated { image_name: NonEmptyStr }
  | MegaRacForeignImagePresented { image_name: String, configurations: String }
  | MegaRacSeveralImagesPresented { configurations: String }
  | MegaRacStaleDetachNotAdmitted { stale_image: String, reason: NonEmptyStr }
  | MegaRacStaleDetachUnconfirmed { detach: MegaRacDetachEvidence, reason: NonEmptyStr }
  | MegaRacRedirectionUncatalogued { image_name: String, wire: Int, configurations: String }
  | MegaRacRefreshClockUnreadable { detail: String }
  | MegaRacNotEnumeratedAfterRefresh { image_name: NonEmptyStr, detach: MegaRacDetachEvidence, standing: RemoteMediaMountStanding }

// THREE INDICES, THREE CONCEPTS, NEVER JOINED. image_list_index is the image's position in
// /remote/images at the look that resolved it (absent on the already-presented route, where no
// listing was consulted); media_index is the virtual device slot; session_index is the redirection
// session. See configuration_row_reading for the nicknaming failure that joining them was.
type MegaRacAttachRoute
  = RouteAlreadyPresented
  | RouteAttached { image_list_index: String }
  | RouteReplaced { image_list_index: String, detach: MegaRacDetachEvidence }

type MegaRacPresentationEvidence {
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity
  image_name: NonEmptyStr
  media_index: String?
  session_index: String?
  redirection_wire: Int
  established_at: EpochMs
  looks: Int
}

// THE STOP COMMAND'S ANSWER AND THE READ-BACK ARE TWO FACTS AND BOTH ARE KEPT. This firmware has
// answered 1411 "Error stopping the remote media redirection" to a stop after which configurations
// read image '' and status 0: the read-back establishes the detach, and the error is retained
// beside it rather than discarded. A success whose read-back still presents the image, or cannot be
// read, establishes nothing.
type StopCommandAnswer {
  success: Bool
  body: String
}

type MegaRacDetachEvidence {
  stale_image: String
  media_index: String
  command: StopCommandAnswer
  readback_read: Bool
  readback: String
}

// WHICH PRESENTED IMAGES THIS ATTACH MAY REPLACE, AND WHETHER IT MAY WRITE ANYTHING DESTRUCTIVE
// NOW. Both are the caller's policy and neither is this operation's to decide: the replaceable set
// is named by a seeded-media STEM, so recognition is the inverse of the naming authority
// (extdeps.provisioning.ubuntu_seeded_install_media ubuntu_seeded_install_media_name_digest_prefix)
// rather than a prefix list authored here; and the admission is established by the caller from its
// own hold and its own power observation. The admission is consulted ONLY when a destructive step
// is needed, so a caller whose host is on still converges the already-attached case as a no-op.
//
// THE DESTRUCTIVE STEP IS stop-media: against a host running from the medium it withdraws what the
// host is reading from, which is why the admission names a host that is off and held.
type MegaRacDetachAdmission
  = MegaRacDetachAdmitted
  | MegaRacDetachNotAdmitted { reason: NonEmptyStr }

type MegaRacReplacementPolicy {
  replaceable_seeded_stem: NonEmptyStr
  detach: MegaRacDetachAdmission
}

// THE CSRF TOKEN IS READ FROM THE PARSED DOCUMENT, not scraped. The shell version matched a regex
// over the response body, which is a second reading of JSON beside the one this repository already
// owns; extdeps.languages.json.parse is the single recognition authority and a document it cannot
// parse is unreadable rather than partially believed.
fn json_string_member(doc: JsonValue, key: String) -> String? {
  match json_object_unique_member(v: doc, key: key) {
    JsonMemberFound { value: v } =>
      match v {
        JsonString { value: s } => Present { value: s }
        _ => none
      }
    _ => none
  }
}

fn json_number_member(doc: JsonValue, key: String) -> String? {
  match json_object_unique_member(v: doc, key: key) {
    JsonMemberFound { value: v } =>
      match v {
        JsonNumber { lexeme: n } => Present { value: n }
        _ => none
      }
    _ => none
  }
}

// THE INDEX OF A NAMED IMAGE, folded over the parsed array. Returns the FIRST match and the fold
// keeps it, because a controller enumerating one name twice is a state this module has never
// observed and would rather report as the index it acted on than silently prefer the last.
fn image_index_named(elements: List<JsonValue>, image_name: String) -> String? {
  fold(elements, init: none, f: (acc, element) =>
    match acc {
      Present { value: _ } => acc
      Absent =>
        match json_string_member(doc: element, key: "image_name") {
          Absent => none
          Present { value: found } =>
            if found == image_name {
              json_number_member(doc: element, key: "image_index")
            } else {
              none
            }
        }
    }
  )
}

fn images_array_elements(doc: JsonValue) -> List<JsonValue>? {
  match doc {
    JsonArray { elements: es } => Present { value: es }
    _ => none
  }
}

// THE START-MEDIA BODY, rendered here rather than by the caller so image_redirection cannot be
// omitted by a caller who does not know it is required. extdeps.bmc.megarac records that omitting
// it makes the firmware refuse with opaque codes 13410/13460, recovered from the firmware's own UI
// bundle rather than from documentation — exactly the kind of fact that is lost when a body is
// assembled at a call site.
fn start_media_body(image_name: NonEmptyStr, image_index: String) -> NonEmptyStr {
  join([
    "{\"image_name\":\"", image_name as String,
    "\",\"image_type\":1,\"image_index\":", image_index,
    ",\"image_redirection\":1}"
  ], "") as NonEmptyStr
}

// THE EFFECT SEQUENCE. Session, list, resolve, start, confirm — and the confirmation is a separate
// read rather than the start call's own answer, for the reason given at the top of this module.
//
// THE CREDENTIAL IS A FILE PATH ON EVERY CALL, INCLUDING OpenSession: curl's --data-urlencode
// password@{password_file} reads the form value from the file, so the password never reaches argv
// (extdeps.bmc.megarac OpenSession). Every subsequent operation carries no credential at all
// because the cookie is the bearer.
//
// AN OPENED SESSION WHOSE TOKEN CANNOT BE READ IS STILL AN ALLOCATED SESSION. An earlier
// revision returned SessionReleaseNotAttempted here, which is the leak that saturated this
// controller: OpenSession succeeded, the cookie was written, and CloseSession never ran because
// the renderer treated the arm as "never opened". The DELETE still needs an X-CSRFTOKEN header
// by the upstream contract; the cookie is the bearer, so the header is supplied as a sentinel
// rather than inventing a second CloseSession shape. A refused or uncertain close remains
// SessionReleaseRefused, never NotAttempted. HTTP 401 after CloseSession is evidence the cookie
// no longer authenticates only when the GET presented a parsed X-CSRFTOKEN; a sentinel header
// makes 401 indistinguishable from header rejection (review 67653).
type SessionCsrfStanding
  = SessionCsrfParsed
  | SessionCsrfUnreadable

fn megarac_session_get_writeout_code(get_body: String) -> String {
  match split(s: get_body, delimiter: "\n").last() {
    Present { value: code } => code
    Absent => ""
  }
}

// WHAT ONE COOKIE-BEARING GET ESTABLISHES, AND NOTHING MORE. The probe is a readonly GET on a
// route THIS firmware serves (the remote-media configurations route, which OpenSession's cookie
// succeeds on moments earlier), with the HTTP status as the trailing line. A succeeding GET is a
// session the controller still recognises; a 401 or 403 is a cookie it no longer names -- the
// ABSENCE observation. GET /api/session is NOT that route on this unit: it answers 404 with a live
// cookie (boots 20 and 21, runs 35437393331 and 35445470385), so a 404 here is the route missing,
// not the session, and is refused as unreadable rather than widened into absent. A mid-body code
// with a different trailer is not a status either.
type SessionPresence
  = SessionPresent
  | SessionAbsent { code: String }
  | SessionPresenceUnreadable { detail: String }

fn megarac_session_presence(get_succeeded: Bool, get_body: String) -> SessionPresence {
  if get_succeeded {
    SessionPresent
  } else {
    let code = megarac_session_get_writeout_code(get_body: get_body)
    if code == "401" || code == "403" {
      SessionAbsent { code: code }
    } else {
      SessionPresenceUnreadable { detail: get_body }
    }
  }
}

// RELEASE IS A TRANSITION, NOT A STATUS. A 4xx AFTER CloseSession proves the cookie is gone only
// if the SAME GET succeeded BEFORE CloseSession: a route that 404s regardless of the cookie, or
// a cookie the controller had already dropped, answers 4xx both times and would otherwise read
// as a clean release -- the absorbing fallback DESIGN section 5 forbids, one status code wide.
// So the fold takes both observations and mints SessionReleased for exactly present -> absent.
// ONE REFUSAL VALUE FOR THE SENTINEL-CSRF CASE, consumed by the re-observation fold and by the
// unreadable-token arm that closes without probing (review 68789: the arm had re-typed the sentence).
data megarac_sentinel_csrf_release_refusal: SessionRelease = SessionReleaseRefused { detail: "the session probe around CloseSession used a sentinel X-CSRFTOKEN because the token was unreadable; a refusal here does not prove the cookie is gone" }

fn megarac_session_release_by_reobservation(
  before: SessionPresence,
  after: SessionPresence,
  csrf: SessionCsrfStanding,
) -> SessionRelease {
  match csrf {
    SessionCsrfUnreadable =>
      megarac_sentinel_csrf_release_refusal
    SessionCsrfParsed =>
      match before {
        SessionPresent =>
          match after {
            SessionAbsent { code: _ } => SessionReleased
            SessionPresent => SessionReleaseRefused { detail: "the session probe still succeeded after CloseSession" }
            SessionPresenceUnreadable { detail: d } =>
              SessionReleaseRefused { detail: concat("the session probe after CloseSession was unreadable; refusing to treat the session as released: ", d) }
          }
        SessionAbsent { code: c } =>
          SessionReleaseRefused { detail: concat("the session probe was already refused BEFORE CloseSession (code ", concat(c, "); a refusal after it proves nothing about release -- the route or the cookie was not observable")) }
        SessionPresenceUnreadable { detail: d } =>
          SessionReleaseRefused { detail: concat("the session probe before CloseSession was unreadable; refusing to adjudicate release: ", d) }
      }
  }
}

fn megarac_close_and_reobserve(
  bmc_host: NonEmptyStr,
  cookie_jar: NonEmptyStr,
  csrf_token: NonEmptyStr,
  csrf: SessionCsrfStanding,
) -> SessionRelease
{
  let before_get = megarac.Media.ProbeSessionOnMediaRoute(
    bmc_host: bmc_host,
    cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
    csrf_token: csrf_token,
  )
  let before = megarac_session_presence(get_succeeded: before_get.success, get_body: before_get.body)
  let _closed = megarac.Media.CloseSession(
    bmc_host: bmc_host,
    cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
    csrf_token: csrf_token,
  )
  let after_get = megarac.Media.ProbeSessionOnMediaRoute(
    bmc_host: bmc_host,
    cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
    csrf_token: csrf_token,
  )
  let after = megarac_session_presence(get_succeeded: after_get.success, get_body: after_get.body)
  return megarac_session_release_by_reobservation(before: before, after: after, csrf: csrf)
}

fn megarac_attach_remote_image(
  bmc_host: NonEmptyStr,
  username: NonEmptyStr,
  password_file: NonEmptyStr,
  cookie_jar: NonEmptyStr,
  image_name: NonEmptyStr,
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity,
  policy: MegaRacReplacementPolicy,
) -> MegaRacAttachResult
  admit_callers: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.machine_intake_mtcollins1_media_attach", decl_name: "mtcollins1_attach_diskless_image"),
  ]
{
  session = megarac.Media.OpenSession(
    bmc_host: bmc_host,
    username: username,
    password_file: password_file,
    cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
  )
  if session.success == false {
    return MegaRacAttachResult {
      outcome: MegaRacSessionRefused { detail: session.body },
      session_release: SessionReleaseNotAttempted,
    }
  }

  let session_doc = match parse_json_document(s: session.body) {
    JsonDocumentParsed { value: v } => some_json_value(v)
    JsonDocumentUnreadable { gap: _ } => none
  }
  let csrf = match session_doc {
    Absent => none
    Present { value: doc } => json_string_member(doc: doc, key: "CSRFToken")
  }

  return match csrf {
    Absent =>
      megarac_release_unreadable_session(
        bmc_host: bmc_host,
        cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
        session_body: session.body,
      )
    Present { value: token } =>
      megarac_attach_then_release(
        bmc_host: bmc_host,
        cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
        csrf_token: token as NonEmptyStr,
        image_name: image_name,
        firmware: firmware,
        policy: policy,
      )
  }
}

// THE CLOSE IS OWED, THE PROBES ARE NOT. With a sentinel X-CSRFTOKEN no probe outcome can prove the
// cookie is gone -- the release fold refuses on SessionCsrfUnreadable before reading either
// observation -- so this arm closes and refuses without spending two round-trips on the one
// transport already known to be misbehaving (review 68750).
fn megarac_release_unreadable_session(
  bmc_host: NonEmptyStr,
  cookie_jar: NonEmptyStr,
  session_body: String,
) -> MegaRacAttachResult
{
  let _closed = megarac.Media.CloseSession(
    bmc_host: bmc_host,
    cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
    csrf_token: "unreadable" as NonEmptyStr,
  )
  return MegaRacAttachResult {
    outcome: MegaRacSessionTokenUnreadable { detail: session_body },
    session_release: megarac_sentinel_csrf_release_refusal,
  }
}

// THE RELEASE RUNS ON EVERY PATH THROUGH THE ATTACH, which is why the attach outcome is computed
// first and the close follows it unconditionally rather than sitting inside a success arm. A
// refusal allocated the same session a success does.
fn megarac_attach_then_release(
  bmc_host: NonEmptyStr,
  cookie_jar: NonEmptyStr,
  csrf_token: NonEmptyStr,
  image_name: NonEmptyStr,
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity,
  policy: MegaRacReplacementPolicy,
) -> MegaRacAttachResult
{
  let outcome = megarac_attach_with_token(
    bmc_host: bmc_host,
    cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
    csrf_token: csrf_token,
    image_name: image_name,
    firmware: firmware,
    policy: policy,
  )

  return MegaRacAttachResult {
    outcome: outcome,
    session_release: megarac_close_and_reobserve(
      bmc_host: bmc_host,
      cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
      csrf_token: csrf_token,
      csrf: SessionCsrfParsed,
    ),
  }
}

// CONFIGURATIONS IS CONSULTED BEFORE ANYTHING IS WRITTEN, so the converged case performs no write
// at all. This is not an optimisation: start-media against an already-presented image is a write
// whose effect on a booted host is unmodelled, and the point of reading first is to not make it.
//
// MALFORMED PRESENTED STATE IS UNKNOWN, NOT "NOT ATTACHED". An earlier revision collapsed a
// JSON parse failure or a non-array document to false, then walked the available-images list
// and could StartMedia over a controller whose current attachment was unreadable. That is the
// absorbing-fallback DESIGN §5 forbids: ignorance rendered as the empty case.
//
// THE OPERATION IS A CONVERGENCE ON ONE DESIRED IMAGE (operator ruling 2026-09-27: "the workflow
// should be ensuring the correct image"). Boot run 36328950865 refused with the previous census
// image still presented and the new one missing from the listing although it was in the export:
// the rmedia daemon enumerates the share when it mounts it. So the step is: the desired image
// presented goes straight to the readiness fold; another image of the caller's replaceable stem
// presented is stopped, under the caller's admission, and read back as gone; the listing is
// re-read and the desired image's CURRENT index resolved; it is attached; and the attach passes the
// same readiness fold. A presented image outside the replaceable stem is somebody else's and
// refuses.
fn megarac_attach_with_token(
  bmc_host: NonEmptyStr,
  cookie_jar: NonEmptyStr,
  csrf_token: NonEmptyStr,
  image_name: NonEmptyStr,
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity,
  policy: MegaRacReplacementPolicy,
) -> MegaRacAttachOutcome
{
  presented = megarac.Media.GetRemoteConfigurations(
    bmc_host: bmc_host,
    cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
    csrf_token: csrf_token,
    max_time: megarac_media_read_max_time_operand(),
  )
  if presented.success == false {
    return MegaRacConfigurationsUnreadable { detail: presented.body }
  }
  let convergence = presented_convergence(
    presented: presented_media(body: presented.body, image_name: image_name, firmware: firmware),
    image_name: image_name,
    replaceable_seeded_stem: policy.replaceable_seeded_stem,
  )
  return match megarac_convergence_step(convergence: convergence, detach: policy.detach, configurations: presented.body) {
    ConvergeStepRefuse { outcome: o } => o
    ConvergeStepAwaitReadiness =>
      megarac_readiness_outcome(
        bmc_host: bmc_host,
        cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
        csrf_token: csrf_token,
        image_name: image_name,
        firmware: firmware,
        route: RouteAlreadyPresented,
        phase: ReadinessOfPresented,
      )
    ConvergeStepDetachStale { row: row } =>
      megarac_detach_then_attach(
        bmc_host: bmc_host,
        cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
        csrf_token: csrf_token,
        image_name: image_name,
        firmware: firmware,
        policy: policy,
        stale: row,
      )
    ConvergeStepAttachFromListing =>
      megarac_attach_from_listing(
        bmc_host: bmc_host,
        cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
        csrf_token: csrf_token,
        image_name: image_name,
        firmware: firmware,
      )
  }
}

// EVERY READ IS BOUNDED, not only the window. A configurations or images GET that hangs would
// otherwise hold the readiness window open past its deadline with no look to judge it by, so each
// call carries curl's --max-time and a call that runs out is one unanswered look.
data megarac_media_read_max_time: Second = second(count: 10)

fn megarac_media_read_max_time_operand() -> NonEmptyStr {
  to_string(second_count(s: megarac_media_read_max_time)) as NonEmptyStr
}

// NOTHING PRESENTED: the listing is consulted as before. With nothing presented there is nothing
// to stop, and stopping is what re-enumerates the share, so an image the listing does not offer
// refuses as it always has.
fn megarac_attach_from_listing(
  bmc_host: NonEmptyStr,
  cookie_jar: NonEmptyStr,
  csrf_token: NonEmptyStr,
  image_name: NonEmptyStr,
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity,
) -> MegaRacAttachOutcome
{
  images = megarac.Media.GetRemoteImages(
    bmc_host: bmc_host,
    cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
    csrf_token: csrf_token,
    max_time: megarac_media_read_max_time_operand(),
  )
  if images.success == false {
    return MegaRacImagesUnreadable { detail: images.body }
  }
  return match images_listing_reading(body: images.body, image_name: image_name) {
    ImagesListingUnparseable { detail: d } => MegaRacImageListingUnparseable { detail: d }
    ImagesListingEmpty => MegaRacImageListingEmpty
    ImagesListingLacks => MegaRacImageNotEnumerated { image_name: image_name }
    ImagesListingOffers { image_index: idx } =>
      megarac_start_then_readiness(
        bmc_host: bmc_host,
        cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
        csrf_token: csrf_token,
        image_name: image_name,
        image_list_index: idx,
        firmware: firmware,
        route: RouteAttached { image_list_index: idx },
      )
  }
}

// THE STOP IS READ BACK BEFORE THE LISTING IS AWAITED, so an attach never follows a stop whose effect
// is unknown. The command's answer and the read-back are both kept (MegaRacDetachEvidence); only the
// read-back decides.
fn megarac_detach_then_attach(
  bmc_host: NonEmptyStr,
  cookie_jar: NonEmptyStr,
  csrf_token: NonEmptyStr,
  image_name: NonEmptyStr,
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity,
  policy: MegaRacReplacementPolicy,
  stale: PresentingRow,
) -> MegaRacAttachOutcome
{
  let media_index = match stale.media_index {
    Present { value: i } => i
    Absent => ""
  }
  if media_index == "" {
    return MegaRacStaleDetachUnconfirmed {
      detach: MegaRacDetachEvidence {
        stale_image: stale.image_name,
        media_index: "",
        command: StopCommandAnswer { success: false, body: "not sent" },
        readback_read: false,
        readback: "",
      },
      reason: "the presenting row carries no media_index, so no stop-media body can name its device; nothing was written",
    }
  }
  let stopped = megarac.Media.StopMedia(
    bmc_host: bmc_host,
    cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
    csrf_token: csrf_token,
    json_body: stop_media_body(image_name: stale.image_name, media_index: media_index),
  )
  let after = megarac.Media.GetRemoteConfigurations(
    bmc_host: bmc_host,
    cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
    csrf_token: csrf_token,
    max_time: megarac_media_read_max_time_operand(),
  )
  let evidence = MegaRacDetachEvidence {
    stale_image: stale.image_name,
    media_index: media_index,
    command: StopCommandAnswer { success: stopped.success, body: stopped.body },
    readback_read: after.success,
    readback: after.body,
  }
  return match detach_verdict(evidence: evidence, image_name: image_name, firmware: firmware, replaceable_seeded_stem: policy.replaceable_seeded_stem) {
    DetachNotEstablished { reason: why } => MegaRacStaleDetachUnconfirmed { detach: evidence, reason: why }
    DetachEstablished =>
      megarac_enumerate_then_attach(
        bmc_host: bmc_host,
        cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
        csrf_token: csrf_token,
        image_name: image_name,
        firmware: firmware,
        detach: evidence,
      )
  }
}

type DetachVerdict
  = DetachEstablished
  | DetachNotEstablished { reason: NonEmptyStr }

// PURE: the detach is established exactly when the read-back was read and presents nothing. The
// command's success is not consulted, in either direction.
fn detach_verdict(
  evidence: MegaRacDetachEvidence,
  image_name: NonEmptyStr,
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity,
  replaceable_seeded_stem: NonEmptyStr,
) -> DetachVerdict {
  if evidence.readback_read == false {
    DetachNotEstablished { reason: "the configurations read-back after stop-media failed, so the stop is unestablished whatever stop-media answered" }
  } else {
    match presented_convergence(
      presented: presented_media(body: evidence.readback, image_name: image_name, firmware: firmware),
      image_name: image_name,
      replaceable_seeded_stem: replaceable_seeded_stem,
    ) {
      ConvergeNothingPresented => DetachEstablished
      _ => DetachNotEstablished { reason: "the configurations read-back after stop-media still presents an image, or cannot be read as presenting nothing" }
    }
  }
}

// STOP-MEDIA IS THE RE-ENUMERATION. Measured on mtcollins1 2026-09-27 with the host off: after
// stop-media cleared the stale presentation, /remote/images listed the newly published census image
// within 15s, while PUT /api/settings/media/general with mount_cd 0 and then 1 was REFUSED both
// times (code 16425, "Error in setting Remote Media Misc Configuration", settings unchanged). So no
// mount_cd cycle is written here: the listing is awaited after the stop, and the index attached is
// the one the CURRENT listing gives the name, never one read before the stop.
fn megarac_enumerate_then_attach(
  bmc_host: NonEmptyStr,
  cookie_jar: NonEmptyStr,
  csrf_token: NonEmptyStr,
  image_name: NonEmptyStr,
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity,
  detach: MegaRacDetachEvidence,
) -> MegaRacAttachOutcome
{
  return match clock_unix_millis_read() {
    ClockUnixMillisRefused { detail: d } => MegaRacRefreshClockUnreadable { detail: d }
    ClockUnixMillisObserved { millis: requested_at } =>
      match megarac_await_enumeration(
        bmc_host: bmc_host,
        cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
        csrf_token: csrf_token,
        image_name: image_name,
        window: RemoteMediaMountWindow { requested_at: requested_at, budget: megarac_refresh_enumeration_budget_ms() },
        observations: [],
        remaining: megarac_refresh_enumeration_ticks(),
      ) {
        EnumerationClockUnreadable { detail: d } => MegaRacRefreshClockUnreadable { detail: d }
        EnumerationUnparseable { detail: d } => MegaRacImageListingUnparseable { detail: d }
        NotEnumeratedAfterRefresh { standing: st } => MegaRacNotEnumeratedAfterRefresh { image_name: image_name, detach: detach, standing: st }
        EnumeratedAfterRefresh { image_index: idx } =>
          megarac_start_then_readiness(
            bmc_host: bmc_host,
            cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
            csrf_token: csrf_token,
            image_name: image_name,
            image_list_index: idx,
            firmware: firmware,
            route: RouteReplaced { image_list_index: idx, detach: detach },
          )
      }
  }
}

// THE STOP-MEDIA BODY. extdeps.bmc.megarac records only that stop-media takes start-media's body
// shape; which index it wants is not recorded anywhere, so this is a typed bet rather than a fact:
// the row's media_index, the virtual device the presentation occupies, since the image enumeration
// index of an attached image is not listed (it has left /remote/images). The read-back decides
// whether the bet held; a wrong index is StaleDetachUnconfirmed, never a success.
fn stop_media_body(image_name: String, media_index: String) -> NonEmptyStr {
  join([
    "{\"image_name\":\"", image_name,
    "\",\"image_type\":1,\"image_index\":", media_index,
    ",\"image_redirection\":1}"
  ], "") as NonEmptyStr
}

// THE RE-ENUMERATION IS A BOUNDED ESTABLISHMENT, folded by gunbc.machine_intake_mount_establishment
// rather than polled until green: the window is declared before the first look, each look is an
// evidenced observation, and a close at the deadline is terminal. The budget is the controller's
// configured retry cadence with margin: rmedia_retry_count 3 at rmedia_retry_interval 15s is 45s,
// and the measured re-enumeration after stop-media took under 15s (2026-09-27).
data megarac_refresh_poll_interval: Second = second(count: 5)

data megarac_refresh_enumeration_budget: Second = second(count: 90)

fn megarac_refresh_enumeration_budget_ms() -> Milliseconds {
  (second_count(s: megarac_refresh_enumeration_budget) as Int) * 1000
}

// One look per interval across the window, plus the look that lands at or past the deadline and
// closes it, so running out of ticks before the window closes is not a reachable exit.
fn megarac_refresh_enumeration_ticks() -> Int {
  (second_count(s: megarac_refresh_enumeration_budget) as Int) / (second_count(s: megarac_refresh_poll_interval) as Int) + 2
}

// WHAT THE WHOLE CONVERGENCE MAY SPEND, for a caller that budgets its step: both windows, each
// window's last bounded call past its deadline, and the reads and writes around them.
fn megarac_convergence_allowance() -> Second {
  let read = second_count(s: megarac_media_read_max_time) as Int
  second(count: (second_count(s: megarac_refresh_enumeration_budget) as Int) + (second_count(s: megarac_refresh_poll_interval) as Int) + read
    + (second_count(s: megarac_readiness_budget) as Int) + (second_count(s: megarac_readiness_interval) as Int) + read
    + 6 * read)
}

type EnumerationAfterRefresh
  = EnumeratedAfterRefresh { image_index: String }
  | NotEnumeratedAfterRefresh { standing: RemoteMediaMountStanding }
  | EnumerationUnparseable { detail: String }
  | EnumerationClockUnreadable { detail: String }

// A LISTING THAT REFUSES IS PENDING, A LISTING THAT PARSES AND LACKS THE NAME IS ABSENT, AND BOTH
// ARE ONE MISS INSIDE THE WINDOW. extdeps.bmc.megarac records that "Could not mount the remote
// path" on the images route means the daemon has not mounted yet; a body that answers but is not a
// JSON array is a protocol failure and refuses at once. The first look is taken at once; the pacing
// sleep runs only between looks that were still pending.
fn megarac_await_enumeration(
  bmc_host: NonEmptyStr,
  cookie_jar: NonEmptyStr,
  csrf_token: NonEmptyStr,
  image_name: NonEmptyStr,
  window: RemoteMediaMountWindow,
  observations: List<RemoteMediaListingObservation>,
  remaining: Int,
) -> EnumerationAfterRefresh
{
  let images = megarac.Media.GetRemoteImages(
    bmc_host: bmc_host,
    cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
    csrf_token: csrf_token,
    max_time: megarac_media_read_max_time_operand(),
  )
  let reading = if images.success { images_listing_reading(body: images.body, image_name: image_name) } else { ImagesListingLacks }
  match clock_unix_millis_read() {
    ClockUnixMillisRefused { detail: d } => EnumerationClockUnreadable { detail: d }
    ClockUnixMillisObserved { millis: now } =>
      match reading {
        ImagesListingUnparseable { detail: d } => EnumerationUnparseable { detail: d }
        _ => {
          let evidence = content_hash_of_value(value: concat("megarac-remote-images:", images.body) as NonEmptyStr)
          let seen = observations.append(RemoteMediaListingObservation {
            observed_at: now,
            listing: images_listing_presence(reading: reading),
            raw_response: evidence,
          })
          let standing = mount_standing_as_of(
            window: window,
            observations: seen,
            boundary: MountEvaluationBoundary { observed_through: now, clock_evidence: evidence },
          )
          match enumeration_decision(standing: standing, reading: reading, remaining: remaining) {
            EnumerationDecided { result: r } => r
            EnumerationLookAgain => {
              let _paced = sleep_delay_seconds_second_carrier_projection(duration: megarac_refresh_poll_interval)
              megarac_await_enumeration(
                bmc_host: bmc_host,
                cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
                csrf_token: csrf_token,
                image_name: image_name,
                window: window,
                observations: seen,
                remaining: remaining - 1,
              )
            }
          }
        }
      }
  }
}

type EnumerationDecision
  = EnumerationDecided { result: EnumerationAfterRefresh }
  | EnumerationLookAgain

// ONLY THE FOLD'S ESTABLISHED STANDING ATTACHES, and only with the index the establishing look read.
// Pending inside the window looks again; every terminal standing is NotEnumeratedAfterRefresh and
// carries the standing that closed it, so a contradiction is reported as one rather than as a miss.
fn enumeration_decision(standing: RemoteMediaMountStanding, reading: ImagesListingReading, remaining: Int) -> EnumerationDecision {
  match standing {
    MountEstablished { established_at: _, establishing_evidence: _ } =>
      match reading {
        ImagesListingOffers { image_index: idx } => EnumerationDecided { result: EnumeratedAfterRefresh { image_index: idx } }
        _ => EnumerationDecided { result: NotEnumeratedAfterRefresh { standing: standing } }
      }
    MountRequested { window: _ } =>
      if remaining > 1 { EnumerationLookAgain } else { EnumerationDecided { result: NotEnumeratedAfterRefresh { standing: standing } } }
    MountPending { window: _, last_observed_at: _, observations: _ } =>
      if remaining > 1 { EnumerationLookAgain } else { EnumerationDecided { result: NotEnumeratedAfterRefresh { standing: standing } } }
    MountTimedOut { window: _, basis: _ } => EnumerationDecided { result: NotEnumeratedAfterRefresh { standing: standing } }
    MountObservationContradictory { cause: _ } => EnumerationDecided { result: NotEnumeratedAfterRefresh { standing: standing } }
  }
}

// THE AVAILABLE-TO-ATTACH LISTING, read once. It lists what may be attached, not what the share
// holds: an attached image has moved to /remote/configurations (see the top of this module).
type ImagesListingReading
  = ImagesListingUnparseable { detail: String }
  | ImagesListingEmpty
  | ImagesListingLacks
  | ImagesListingOffers { image_index: String }

fn images_listing_reading(body: String, image_name: NonEmptyStr) -> ImagesListingReading {
  match parse_json_document(s: body) {
    JsonDocumentUnreadable { gap: _ } => ImagesListingUnparseable { detail: body }
    JsonDocumentParsed { value: v } =>
      match images_array_elements(doc: v) {
        Absent => ImagesListingUnparseable { detail: body }
        Present { value: elements } =>
          if (elements |> count) == 0 {
            ImagesListingEmpty
          } else {
            match image_index_named(elements: elements, image_name: image_name as String) {
              Absent => ImagesListingLacks
              Present { value: idx } => ImagesListingOffers { image_index: idx }
            }
          }
      }
  }
}

fn images_listing_presence(reading: ImagesListingReading) -> RemoteMediaListing {
  match reading {
    ImagesListingOffers { image_index: _ } => MediaImageListed
    _ => MediaImageAbsentFromListing
  }
}

// ONE PRESENTING ROW: this CD device is presenting this name, with redirection started or
// connecting. media_index is the virtual device slot, carried for the stop-media body only and
// never compared against an image index (the nicknaming note on configuration_row_reading).
type PresentingRow {
  image_name: String
  media_index: String?
  session_index: String?
  redirection_wire: Int
  redirection: MegaRacRedirectionStatus
}

// THE CONFIRMATION READS EXACT ACTIVE ROWS, not a substring of a body. An earlier form asked
// whether the configurations text CONTAINED the image name, which admits a stopped configuration
// that still names it, and admits an error body that happens to mention it.
//
// THE INDEX IS DELIBERATELY NOT COMPARED, and an earlier revision of this check did compare it —
// first reading image_index, which is absent here so every genuine attachment was reported
// unconfirmed, then reading media_index, which is present and agrees. The second spelling passed,
// and it was still wrong: media_index is the VIRTUAL CD DEVICE SLOT, alongside session_index, not a
// position in the image enumeration. It agreed with the resolved image_index only because this unit
// presents a single CD device, so both are 0. Comparing them is the §3 nicknaming failure — two
// unrelated concepts joined because they share a coincidence and half a name — and it would have
// started refusing the moment a controller offered a second slot, with a message blaming the image.
//
// EVERY PRESENTING ROW IS READ, NOT ONLY THE ONE NAMING THE DESIRED IMAGE, because convergence
// decides over what else is presented. A named row whose status is unparseable, uncatalogued for
// the firmware, or uncatalogued on the wire is unread — not "not presenting" — and the whole
// document is then unreadable, so neither a stop nor a start is licensed over it. A row that names
// no image and is not presenting is an idle device. A non-CD row naming the desired image is
// unreadable; a non-CD row naming anything else is outside this CD lane.
type ConfigurationRowReading
  = ConfigurationRowUnreadable { detail: String }
  | ConfigurationRowUncatalogued { image_name: String, wire: Int }
  | ConfigurationRowPresenting { row: PresentingRow }
  | ConfigurationRowIdle

fn configuration_row_reading(
  row: JsonValue,
  image_name: NonEmptyStr,
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity,
) -> ConfigurationRowReading {
  let name = match json_string_member(doc: row, key: "image_name") {
    Present { value: n } => n
    Absent => ""
  }
  match json_number_member(doc: row, key: "media_type") {
    Absent =>
      if name == "" { ConfigurationRowIdle } else { ConfigurationRowUnreadable { detail: concat("media_type missing on a row that names ", name) } }
    Present { value: mt } =>
      if mt != "1" {
        if name == (image_name as String) {
          ConfigurationRowUnreadable { detail: "a row names the image but is not CD media_type 1" }
        } else {
          ConfigurationRowIdle
        }
      } else {
        match json_number_member(doc: row, key: "redirection_status") {
          Absent =>
            if name == "" { ConfigurationRowIdle } else { ConfigurationRowUnreadable { detail: concat("redirection_status missing on a row that names ", name) } }
          Present { value: st } =>
            match parse_int(s: st) {
              Absent => ConfigurationRowUnreadable { detail: concat("redirection_status is not an integer: ", st) }
              Present { value: wire } =>
                match megarac_redirection_status_of_wire(firmware: firmware, wire: wire) {
                  RedirectionStatusFirmwareUncatalogued { firmware: _, wire: w } =>
                    if name == "" { ConfigurationRowIdle } else { ConfigurationRowUncatalogued { image_name: name, wire: w } }
                  RedirectionStatusKnown { firmware: _, status: status } =>
                    match status {
                      RedirectionStopped => ConfigurationRowIdle
                      RedirectionWireUncatalogued { wire: w } =>
                        if name == "" { ConfigurationRowIdle } else { ConfigurationRowUncatalogued { image_name: name, wire: w } }
                      _ =>
                        if name == "" {
                          ConfigurationRowUnreadable { detail: "a CD row is presenting but names no image" }
                        } else {
                          ConfigurationRowPresenting {
                            row: PresentingRow {
                              image_name: name,
                              media_index: json_number_member(doc: row, key: "media_index"),
                              session_index: json_number_member(doc: row, key: "session_index"),
                              redirection_wire: wire,
                              redirection: status,
                            },
                          }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
      }
  }
}

type PresentedMedia
  = PresentedMediaDocumentUnreadable { detail: String }
  | PresentedMediaUncatalogued { image_name: String, wire: Int }
  | PresentedMediaRead { presenting: List<PresentingRow> }

fn presented_media(
  body: String,
  image_name: NonEmptyStr,
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity,
) -> PresentedMedia {
  match parse_json_document(s: body) {
    JsonDocumentUnreadable { gap: _ } => PresentedMediaDocumentUnreadable { detail: body }
    JsonDocumentParsed { value: v } =>
      match images_array_elements(doc: v) {
        Absent => PresentedMediaDocumentUnreadable { detail: body }
        Present { value: rows } =>
          fold(rows, init: PresentedMediaRead { presenting: [] }, f: (acc, row) =>
            match acc {
              PresentedMediaDocumentUnreadable { detail: _ } => acc
              PresentedMediaUncatalogued { image_name: _, wire: _ } => acc
              PresentedMediaRead { presenting: ps } =>
                match configuration_row_reading(row: row, image_name: image_name, firmware: firmware) {
                  ConfigurationRowUnreadable { detail: d } => PresentedMediaDocumentUnreadable { detail: d }
                  ConfigurationRowUncatalogued { image_name: n, wire: w } => PresentedMediaUncatalogued { image_name: n, wire: w }
                  ConfigurationRowIdle => acc
                  ConfigurationRowPresenting { row: r } => PresentedMediaRead { presenting: ps.append(r) }
                }
            }
          )
      }
  }
}

// WHAT IS PRESENTED, RELATIVE TO THE DESIRED IMAGE AND THE REPLACEABLE STEM. The desired image
// presented goes to the readiness fold, which is where duplicate or mixed rows are judged.
// Otherwise any presented image the stem's naming inverse does not recognise is foreign and
// decides the answer; this unit presents one CD device, so two replaceable images presented at
// once is a state never observed and refuses rather than being stopped in some order.
type PresentedConvergence
  = ConvergeUnreadable { detail: String }
  | ConvergeUncatalogued { image_name: String, wire: Int }
  | ConvergeDesiredPresented
  | ConvergeNothingPresented
  | ConvergeStalePresented { row: PresentingRow }
  | ConvergeForeignPresented { image_name: String }
  | ConvergeSeveralPresented

fn presented_convergence(
  presented: PresentedMedia,
  image_name: NonEmptyStr,
  replaceable_seeded_stem: NonEmptyStr,
) -> PresentedConvergence {
  match presented {
    PresentedMediaDocumentUnreadable { detail: d } => ConvergeUnreadable { detail: d }
    PresentedMediaUncatalogued { image_name: n, wire: w } => ConvergeUncatalogued { image_name: n, wire: w }
    PresentedMediaRead { presenting: ps } =>
      if ps |> any(r => r.image_name == (image_name as String)) {
        ConvergeDesiredPresented
      } else {
        fold(ps, init: ConvergeNothingPresented, f: (acc, r) =>
          match acc {
            ConvergeForeignPresented { image_name: _ } => acc
            _ =>
              match ubuntu_seeded_install_media_name_digest_prefix(image_stem: replaceable_seeded_stem, image_name: r.image_name) {
                Absent => ConvergeForeignPresented { image_name: r.image_name }
                Present { value: _ } =>
                  match acc {
                    ConvergeNothingPresented => ConvergeStalePresented { row: r }
                    _ => ConvergeSeveralPresented
                  }
              }
          }
        )
      }
  }
}

type ConvergenceStep
  = ConvergeStepAwaitReadiness
  | ConvergeStepRefuse { outcome: MegaRacAttachOutcome }
  | ConvergeStepDetachStale { row: PresentingRow }
  | ConvergeStepAttachFromListing

// THE DECISION, PURE, so every control is a supplied configurations reading rather than a
// controller. The admission is read only on the arm that would write destructively: a host that is
// on with the desired image presented makes no write, and goes to the readiness fold like any other
// presentation.
fn megarac_convergence_step(
  convergence: PresentedConvergence,
  detach: MegaRacDetachAdmission,
  configurations: String,
) -> ConvergenceStep {
  match convergence {
    ConvergeUnreadable { detail: d } => ConvergeStepRefuse { outcome: MegaRacConfigurationsUnreadable { detail: d } }
    ConvergeUncatalogued { image_name: n, wire: w } => ConvergeStepRefuse { outcome: MegaRacRedirectionUncatalogued { image_name: n, wire: w, configurations: configurations } }
    ConvergeDesiredPresented => ConvergeStepAwaitReadiness
    ConvergeNothingPresented => ConvergeStepAttachFromListing
    ConvergeForeignPresented { image_name: n } => ConvergeStepRefuse { outcome: MegaRacForeignImagePresented { image_name: n, configurations: configurations } }
    ConvergeSeveralPresented => ConvergeStepRefuse { outcome: MegaRacSeveralImagesPresented { configurations: configurations } }
    ConvergeStalePresented { row: r } =>
      match detach {
        MegaRacDetachAdmitted => ConvergeStepDetachStale { row: r }
        MegaRacDetachNotAdmitted { reason: why } => ConvergeStepRefuse { outcome: MegaRacStaleDetachNotAdmitted { stale_image: r.image_name, reason: why } }
      }
  }
}

// A NON-ZERO START IS NOT A REFUSAL, and this firmware is why: the same controller answers HTTP 500
// on writes that take effect, and its mount daemon is asynchronous. The readiness fold decides.
fn megarac_start_then_readiness(
  bmc_host: NonEmptyStr,
  cookie_jar: NonEmptyStr,
  csrf_token: NonEmptyStr,
  image_name: NonEmptyStr,
  image_list_index: String,
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity,
  route: MegaRacAttachRoute,
) -> MegaRacAttachOutcome
{
  let _start = megarac.Media.StartMedia(
    bmc_host: bmc_host,
    cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
    csrf_token: csrf_token,
    json_body: start_media_body(image_name: image_name, image_index: image_list_index),
  )
  return megarac_readiness_outcome(
    bmc_host: bmc_host,
    cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
    csrf_token: csrf_token,
    image_name: image_name,
    firmware: firmware,
    route: route,
    phase: ReadinessAfterStart,
  )
}

// ─── READINESS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// THE POLICY, AND WHY IT IS NOT THE FIRMWARE'S STATE. Boot run 36330382023 read configurations
// 0.11s after start-media and powered on 0.7s later; the firmware printed "Boot option loading
// failed" and fell to the UEFI shell, and configurations afterwards read status 16, session_index
// 255. So the POLICY here is: only STARTED, on exactly one CD row naming the intended image, with a
// bound session, is ready. CONNECTING is pending and is observed again within the window. That is a
// readiness policy, not a claim that 100 never serves: a boot on this unit once reached GRUB from a
// session that still read 100 (extdeps.bmc.megarac megarac_redirection_presentation_standing keeps
// Connecting as presenting, and this does not redefine it). The manual re-attach of 2026-09-27 read
// 100 at +6s and 1 with session_index 0 from +12s, stable to +120s, so waiting for Started costs
// seconds and buys the state a boot is known to succeed from.
//
// NOT PRESENTED is pending only after this attempt's own start-media — the admitted establishment
// transition. On the already-presented route the row was just seen, so its disappearance is a
// withdrawal nobody here requested and refuses.
//
// UNCATALOGUED, MALFORMED, AMBIGUOUS OR WRONG refuse at once with the evidence: an uncatalogued
// wire keeps its number, duplicate rows naming the image and a row presenting a different image
// keep the configurations document. Decoder ignorance is not a retry cue.
type ReadinessPhase
  = ReadinessAfterStart
  | ReadinessOfPresented

type AttachReadiness
  = ReadinessStarted { row: PresentingRow }
  | ReadinessConnecting { row: PresentingRow }
  | ReadinessStartedUnbound { row: PresentingRow }
  | ReadinessNotPresented { configurations: String }
  | ReadinessUnanswered { detail: String }
  | ReadinessUncatalogued { image_name: String, wire: Int, configurations: String }
  | ReadinessMalformed { detail: String }
  | ReadinessDuplicate { configurations: String }
  | ReadinessWrongPresentation { image_name: String, configurations: String }

type ReadinessLook {
  observed_at: EpochMs
  reading: AttachReadiness
}

// THE SESSION IS BOUND WHEN session_index NAMES A SLOT. 255 is what the failed boot's row carried
// beside status 16, and an unsigned byte at its maximum is the usual "no slot" sentinel; that it
// means unbound on this firmware is a typed bet from one observation, not a documented fact, and
// it errs toward waiting rather than toward powering on.
data megarac_unbound_session_index: Int = 255

fn presenting_session_bound(row: PresentingRow) -> Bool {
  match row.session_index {
    Absent => false
    Present { value: s } =>
      match parse_int(s: s) {
        Absent => false
        Present { value: n } => n >= 0 && n < megarac_unbound_session_index
      }
  }
}

// ONE LOOK, PURE, over one configurations answer, so every control is a supplied body.
fn attach_readiness(
  answered: Bool,
  body: String,
  image_name: NonEmptyStr,
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity,
) -> AttachReadiness {
  if answered == false {
    ReadinessUnanswered { detail: body }
  } else {
    match presented_media(body: body, image_name: image_name, firmware: firmware) {
      PresentedMediaDocumentUnreadable { detail: d } => ReadinessMalformed { detail: d }
      PresentedMediaUncatalogued { image_name: n, wire: w } => ReadinessUncatalogued { image_name: n, wire: w, configurations: body }
      PresentedMediaRead { presenting: ps } => {
        let named = ps |> filter(r => r.image_name == (image_name as String))
        let others = ps |> filter(r => r.image_name != (image_name as String))
        if (others |> count) > 0 {
          match others.first() {
            Present { value: o } => ReadinessWrongPresentation { image_name: o.image_name, configurations: body }
            Absent => ReadinessMalformed { detail: body }
          }
        } else if (named |> count) > 1 {
          ReadinessDuplicate { configurations: body }
        } else {
          match named.first() {
            Absent => ReadinessNotPresented { configurations: body }
            Present { value: r } =>
              match r.redirection {
                RedirectionStartedConnectionAccepted =>
                  if presenting_session_bound(row: r) { ReadinessStarted { row: r } } else { ReadinessStartedUnbound { row: r } }
                _ => ReadinessConnecting { row: r }
              }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

type ReadinessStanding
  = ReadinessEstablished { look: ReadinessLook }
  | ReadinessPending
  | ReadinessRefusedAt { look: ReadinessLook }

// THE ONE-LOOK STANDING, pure. Pending is representable only for readings the policy calls
// transitional, and not-presented only in the start phase. An unanswered GET (curl ran out of its
// --max-time, or the controller answered 5xx mid-transition) is one miss, not evidence either way.
fn readiness_standing(look: ReadinessLook, phase: ReadinessPhase) -> ReadinessStanding {
  match look.reading {
    ReadinessStarted { row: _ } => ReadinessEstablished { look: look }
    ReadinessConnecting { row: _ } => ReadinessPending
    ReadinessStartedUnbound { row: _ } => ReadinessPending
    ReadinessUnanswered { detail: _ } => ReadinessPending
    ReadinessNotPresented { configurations: _ } =>
      match phase {
        ReadinessAfterStart => ReadinessPending
        ReadinessOfPresented => ReadinessRefusedAt { look: look }
      }
    _ => ReadinessRefusedAt { look: look }
  }
}

type ReadinessVerdict
  = ReadinessReady { look: ReadinessLook, looks: Int }
  | ReadinessLookAgain
  | ReadinessWindowClosed { last: ReadinessLook, deadline: EpochMs, looks: Int }
  | ReadinessRefusedVerdict { look: ReadinessLook, looks: Int }

// THE WINDOW IS HALF-OPEN AND DECLARED BEFORE THE FIRST LOOK: opened_at <= observed_at < deadline.
// A Started look at or past the deadline does not establish readiness — it is outside the window
// the policy was declared over — and a refusal reading refuses whenever it is seen.
fn readiness_verdict(
  opened_at: EpochMs,
  budget: Milliseconds,
  look: ReadinessLook,
  phase: ReadinessPhase,
  looks: Int,
) -> ReadinessVerdict {
  let deadline = opened_at + budget
  match readiness_standing(look: look, phase: phase) {
    ReadinessRefusedAt { look: l } => ReadinessRefusedVerdict { look: l, looks: looks }
    ReadinessEstablished { look: l } =>
      if l.observed_at < deadline { ReadinessReady { look: l, looks: looks } } else { ReadinessWindowClosed { last: l, deadline: deadline, looks: looks } }
    ReadinessPending =>
      if look.observed_at < deadline { ReadinessLookAgain } else { ReadinessWindowClosed { last: look, deadline: deadline, looks: looks } }
  }
}

data megarac_readiness_budget: Second = second(count: 30)

data megarac_readiness_interval: Second = second(count: 2)

fn megarac_readiness_budget_ms() -> Milliseconds {
  (second_count(s: megarac_readiness_budget) as Int) * 1000
}

type ReadinessWait
  = ReadinessWaitReady { look: ReadinessLook, looks: Int }
  | ReadinessWaitClosed { last: ReadinessLook, deadline: EpochMs, looks: Int }
  | ReadinessWaitRefused { look: ReadinessLook, looks: Int }
  | ReadinessWaitClockUnreadable { detail: String }

// THE WAIT: read at once, and pace only between looks that were pending. The window is judged by the
// clock read beside each look; each look's GET is bounded by --max-time, so no single call can hold
// the window open.
fn megarac_await_readiness(
  bmc_host: NonEmptyStr,
  cookie_jar: NonEmptyStr,
  csrf_token: NonEmptyStr,
  image_name: NonEmptyStr,
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity,
  phase: ReadinessPhase,
  opened_at: EpochMs,
  looks: Int,
) -> ReadinessWait
{
  let got = megarac.Media.GetRemoteConfigurations(
    bmc_host: bmc_host,
    cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
    csrf_token: csrf_token,
    max_time: megarac_media_read_max_time_operand(),
  )
  match clock_unix_millis_read() {
    ClockUnixMillisRefused { detail: d } => ReadinessWaitClockUnreadable { detail: d }
    ClockUnixMillisObserved { millis: now } => {
      let look = ReadinessLook { observed_at: now, reading: attach_readiness(answered: got.success, body: got.body, image_name: image_name, firmware: firmware) }
      match readiness_verdict(opened_at: opened_at, budget: megarac_readiness_budget_ms(), look: look, phase: phase, looks: looks + 1) {
        ReadinessReady { look: l, looks: n } => ReadinessWaitReady { look: l, looks: n }
        ReadinessWindowClosed { last: l, deadline: d, looks: n } => ReadinessWaitClosed { last: l, deadline: d, looks: n }
        ReadinessRefusedVerdict { look: l, looks: n } => ReadinessWaitRefused { look: l, looks: n }
        ReadinessLookAgain => {
          let _paced = sleep_delay_seconds_second_carrier_projection(duration: megarac_readiness_interval)
          megarac_await_readiness(
            bmc_host: bmc_host,
            cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
            csrf_token: csrf_token,
            image_name: image_name,
            firmware: firmware,
            phase: phase,
            opened_at: opened_at,
            looks: looks + 1,
          )
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

fn megarac_readiness_outcome(
  bmc_host: NonEmptyStr,
  cookie_jar: NonEmptyStr,
  csrf_token: NonEmptyStr,
  image_name: NonEmptyStr,
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity,
  route: MegaRacAttachRoute,
  phase: ReadinessPhase,
) -> MegaRacAttachOutcome
{
  return match clock_unix_millis_read() {
    ClockUnixMillisRefused { detail: d } => MegaRacReadinessClockUnreadable { image_name: image_name, route: route, detail: d }
    ClockUnixMillisObserved { millis: opened_at } =>
      readiness_wait_outcome(
        wait: megarac_await_readiness(
          bmc_host: bmc_host,
          cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
          csrf_token: csrf_token,
          image_name: image_name,
          firmware: firmware,
          phase: phase,
          opened_at: opened_at,
          looks: 0,
        ),
        image_name: image_name,
        firmware: firmware,
        route: route,
      )
  }
}

// PURE: the wait's answer as the attach outcome. Only a Started look reaches MegaRacPresentationReady,
// and the evidence is read from that look's row, so the record a boot is gated on is the row that
// satisfied the policy.
fn readiness_wait_outcome(
  wait: ReadinessWait,
  image_name: NonEmptyStr,
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity,
  route: MegaRacAttachRoute,
) -> MegaRacAttachOutcome {
  match wait {
    ReadinessWaitClockUnreadable { detail: d } => MegaRacReadinessClockUnreadable { image_name: image_name, route: route, detail: d }
    ReadinessWaitClosed { last: l, deadline: d, looks: n } => MegaRacReadinessTimedOut { image_name: image_name, route: route, last: l, deadline: d, looks: n }
    ReadinessWaitRefused { look: l, looks: n } => MegaRacReadinessRefused { image_name: image_name, route: route, look: l, looks: n }
    ReadinessWaitReady { look: l, looks: n } =>
      match l.reading {
        ReadinessStarted { row: r } =>
          MegaRacPresentationReady {
            route: route,
            evidence: MegaRacPresentationEvidence {
              firmware: firmware,
              image_name: image_name,
              media_index: r.media_index,
              session_index: r.session_index,
              redirection_wire: r.redirection_wire,
              established_at: l.observed_at,
              looks: n,
            },
          }
        _ => MegaRacReadinessRefused { image_name: image_name, route: route, look: l, looks: n }
      }
  }
}
